 "notes": [
  "dc CALL 2026-10-28 Q3 2026 earnings call (AV transcript read: CFO prepared remarks, Q&A on AI pricing, cRPO, delivery expertise, capex)",
  "dc SEGMENT one operating and reportable segment (CODM = CEO), 10-Q Note 19; segments here are revenue lines (subscription, professional services), not reportable segments",
  "dc DOC results of 2026-10-28 are 4 days before as_of 2026-11-01 and citable from 2026-10-30; the call transcript (AV) is dated 2026-10-28 likewise",
  "dc MGMT (CFO, call) subscription revenue beat passed through half to FY guide (all FX plus half of Q3 beat); the rest withheld because delivery-expertise services for select large AI deals are carved out of subscription revenue into professional services: about 25 bp of growth in Q3, about 50 bp expected in Q4; value returns to subscription on renewal; management does not expect to include it long term",
  "dc MGMT (CFO, call) Q4 cRPO growth guide 18.5% cc is lower because about half of Q3's cRPO beat came from early renewals pulled from Q4, a higher on-prem mix from public sector (about 25 bp headwind to Q4 cRPO, still lands in revenue) and a rising T4C backlog that counts in revenue but not cRPO",
  "dc MGMT (CEO/CFO) AI ACV target raised twice in 2026, from $1.0B at start of year to $1.7B by end of 2026; AI net new ACV +65% y/y in Q3; AI deals above $1M grew 4.5x y/y; management target: AI 30% of ACV by 2030; long-term Rule of 60+",
  "dc MGMT (CFO) FY2026 free cash flow margin target raised from 35% to 36% on lower capex (about 3% of revenue); acquisitions' margin dilution fully offset, FY non-GAAP operating margin 31.5% (+50 bp y/y)",
  "dc MGMT (CFO) customers are happy with hybrid seat plus consumption pricing and are not asking for outcome-based pricing (answer to analyst question)",
  "dc MGMT (CEO) Q3 net new ACV: business and consumer services over 3x y/y, technology nearly +40%; US federal deals above $1M +30% y/y and federal net new ACV growth expected to accelerate in Q4; asset management crossed $1B ACV; 19 deals above $5M net new ACV (+135% y/y)",
  "dc FACT cRPO growth 20.5% reported / 21% cc includes Armis (closed 2026-04-20) and Moveworks (closed 2025-12-15) contribution; the organic rate is not disclosed in the documents read (analyst on the call called organic cRPO stable to modestly decelerating); gap: no organic cRPO figure",
  "dc FACT GAAP operating margin Q3 2026 9.5% vs 17% a year earlier: amortization of purchased intangibles $198M (5% of revenue vs 1%), severance $87M, business combination costs $35M, SBC $633M (15.5%); non-GAAP margin 32.5% vs 33.5%",
  "dc FACT balance sheet 2026-09-30: cash 2,393M and marketable securities 2,214M current plus 2,354M long-term, strategic investments 2,050M; debt carrying 7,524M (short-term 2,086M incl. commercial paper 2.1B principal at 4.05% weighted rate, 62 days; long-term 5,438M; senior notes 5.5B principal due May 2028 to May 2056 incl. 1.5B 1.40% due 2030); goodwill 10.0B and intangibles 3.6B after Armis (7.6B cash), Veza (about 1.2B), Moveworks (2.4B)",
  "dc FACT no share repurchases in Q3 2026; 9M 2026 repurchases 2,225M incl. 2.0B ASR in Q1; 4.2B authorization remaining; diluted shares 1,043M Q3, guided 1.05B for Q4 (five-for-one split effective 2025-12-17, periods restated)",
  "dc FACT RPO 29.7B, about 46% to be recognized within 12 months, the majority of the rest over months 13 to 36; RPO excludes arrears-billed contracts; average contract duration is lengthening per CFO",
  "dc FACT purchase commitments (10-Q Note 9): cloud services 262M rest of 2026, 432M 2027, 606M 2028, 737M 2029, 2.8B 2030; IT equipment provider about 1.6B through 2030; leases not yet commenced 355M; unrecognized tax benefits 197M",
  "dc FACT largest customer: a U.S. federal channel partner and systems integrator, 12% of revenue in Q3 and 9M 2026 (11% in FY2025 and 9M 2025) and 20% of receivables (11% at 2025 year end); management reports no collection concerns",
  "dc FACT guidance track: subscription revenue beat the guided midpoint in all 7 quarters read (+0.3% to +2.7%); the Q2 2025 row (guide 3,030-3,035 in the Q1 2025 release vs actual 3,113) is recorded as printed in the release text",
  "dc RISK platform/AI: failure to innovate and adapt in an intensely competitive market, AI incorporation risk (operational, legal, ethical); 10-K Item 1A summary, risks related to ability to grow",
  "dc RISK public sector: government procurement and contracting rules; a U.S. federal channel partner is 12% of revenue; DOJ investigation of 2023 hire of the Army CIO (resignation of President and COO July 2024; outcome and cost cannot be predicted, 10-Q Note 9 Other)",
  "dc RISK acquisitions: Armis 7.6B, Veza 1.2B, Moveworks 2.4B in 10 months, integration and dilution risk; 10-K Item 1A (as we acquire or invest in companies), goodwill 10.0B",
  "dc RISK leverage: debt rose from 1.5B to 7.5B in 2026 (commercial paper 2.1B maturing within about 62 days, refinancing and rate risk); 10-K Item 1A debt service obligations",
  "dc RISK growth deceleration: management guides Q4 cRPO growth 18.5% cc (from 21% in Q3); 10-K Item 1A 'we expect our revenue growth rate to decline over the long term'",
  "dc RISK cyber and platform availability: a security event or service disruption could cost customers and create liability; 10-K Item 1A operation risks",
  "dc RISK partners and deal complexity: reliance on partners for a rising share of revenue; larger deals bring longer cycles, pricing pressure and implementation challenges (10-K Item 1A)",
